# Under the checking word FlowFixpoint Link goes over its flow once more when it is at rest: every edge is gone along and every observer told as if for the first time. Where a node climbs, a rule had not laid down again what it owed, and the build stops by name (FlowEndedTooEarly).
# The program is one in which a read is told again when a member comes later: the flow is closed, so the tables are written as without the word.
# OPTIONS: check=FlowFixpoint
# PROGRAM-OF: sets/a-read-is-told-again-when-a-member-comes-later.ir
# RUN: link functions mechanisms=all
# CHECK-NOT: FlowEndedTooEarly
# CHECK: function f0
